   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hello everyone,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m new to lavaan (and SEM in general) so I went through the tutorial and I see that in the CFA example the chi-square has a value of 85.306 (df=24, P=0.000) while in the SEM example the chi-square has a value of 38.125 (df=35, P=0.329). Does this mean that in the CFA we reject the null hypothesis and in the SEM we don&#39;t? Thus, can we say that the SEM model has a good fit but the CFA doesn&#39;t?</div><div><br></div><div>I would appreciate any help understanding how the goodness of fit works in these two cases.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
