  {
   "id": "OFDb6w_iAQAJ",
   "from": "Rönkkö, Mikko",
   "author": "bfa43814f6ba1969",
   "date": "2022-06-08T19:34:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: goodness of fit",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"en-FI\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">If two different  models are fit to two different data, then it does not make sense to compare model fit.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">The question of chi2 p-value is a bit controversial. There are two extremes:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<ol style=\"margin-top:0cm\" start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\r\n<li style=\"margin-left:0cm\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">chi2 is valid test and if a model has p &lt;.05, it is not the correct model for the data and should not be interpreted<u></u><u></u></span></li><li style=\"margin-left:0cm\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Models tend to be approximations of reality but never perfect representations. Therefore, models should not be tested for exact fit and\r\n the chi2 test that does just that should not be used at all.<u></u><u></u></span></li></ol>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">You can find a lot of fights between the proponents of these two perspectives on the SEMNET email list.  Here is my take on the issue:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/L-mjMlyl2Xg?t=563\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://youtu.be/L-mjMlyl2Xg?t%3D563&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792417672791000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FxGUtbtdPa9ojbirULsL5\">https://youtu.be/L-mjMlyl2Xg?t=563</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">What I think that if p &lt;.05 you should do is to do diagnostics to see if the model is misspecified in a way that makes a difference. If p &gt;.05, you can congratulate yourself for finding a rare\r\n case of model that fits close to exactly. But you still should do diagnostics. Kline 2011, chapter 8 provides an excellent discussion on this issue.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"en-FI\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Mikko<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;margin-left:36.0pt\">\r\n<b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">From: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\"><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Socrates Dimitriadis &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">em...@socrates.name</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Wednesday, 8. June 2022 at 16.50<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>lavaan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Re: goodness of fit<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Hi Mikko and thank you for your prompt reply. Here are the two links. But the two models are not using the same dataset, so they&#39;re not comparable. However, given that they&#39;re provided\r\n as examples of the &quot;official&quot; tutorial, it&#39;s kind of confusing what a good fit is. Should our goal be the rejection of the null or not? Is there any rule of thumb for the value of P (chi-square test) that is considered acceptable?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792417672791000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ouZnQODAVlWQb3k1OMdpp\">https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/sem.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/sem.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792417672791000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0JF7pqQBUdEwcf-YBjo_au\">https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/sem.html</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">thanks<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Socrates<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">On Wednesday, June 8, 2022 at 2:46:57 AM UTC-4 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mikko....@jyu.fi</a> wrote:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-top:5.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Hi,</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Can you link to the examples? SEM model is typically nested in CFA and should not fit better than the CFA model.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Mikko</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">From: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\"><span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a></span> &lt;<span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a></span>&gt; on behalf of Socrates Dimitriadis\r\n &lt;<span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">em...@socrates.name</a></span>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Wednesday, 8. June 2022 at 8.57<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>lavaan &lt;<span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a></span>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>goodness of fit</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Hello everyone,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">I&#39;m new to lavaan (and SEM in general) so I went through the tutorial and I see that in the CFA example the chi-square has a value of 85.306 (df=24, P=0.000) while in the SEM example the chi-square has a value of 38.125 (df=35,\r\n P=0.329). Does this mean that in the CFA we reject the null hypothesis and in the SEM we don&#39;t? Thus, can we say that the SEM model has a good fit but the CFA doesn&#39;t?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">I would appreciate any help understanding how the goodness of fit works in these two cases.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Thank you!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a></span>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit </span><a href=\"https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgroups.google.com%2Fd%2Fmsgid%2Flavaan%2F5aac5871-dc63-4712-bf35-ba0b6672dbb9n%2540googlegroups.com%3Futm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;data=05%7C01%7C%7C27a1b53e01994270de7e08da4955ab3d%7Ce9662d58caa44bc1b138c8b1acab5a11%7C1%7C0%7C637902930569664309%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=XWoQQfGsqRCmVkGjTq6viTu8ecg92CY8P9DR8vPEibk%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fgroups.google.com%252Fd%252Fmsgid%252Flavaan%252F5aac5871-dc63-4712-bf35-ba0b6672dbb9n%252540googlegroups.com%253Futm_medium%253Demail%2526utm_source%253Dfooter%26data%3D05%257C01%257C%257C27a1b53e01994270de7e08da4955ab3d%257Ce9662d58caa44bc1b138c8b1acab5a11%257C1%257C0%257C637902930569664309%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C3000%257C%257C%257C%26sdata%3DXWoQQfGsqRCmVkGjTq6viTu8ecg92CY8P9DR8vPEibk%253D%26reserved%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792417672791000&amp;usg=AOvVaw039Wo4wzH4ySrogBb2VlPy\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/lavaan/5aac5871-dc63-4712-bf35-ba0b6672dbb9n%40googlegroups.com</span></a><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
